31
00:02:15,973 --> 00:02:18,471
over time, based on various, you know, intuitive

32
00:02:18,471 --> 00:02:22,219
price actions we see on the ladder over a period of time.

33
00:02:22,220 --> 00:02:26,429
And it's that intuition, that feeling, that confidence, that trust,

34
00:02:26,429 --> 00:02:31,059
all of that together equals a probability of an outcome, okay?

35
00:02:31,060 --> 00:02:33,780
So, just bear with me when I use that word probability.

36
00:02:33,780 --> 00:02:35,790
It's not in the most technical sense.

37
00:02:35,790 --> 00:02:39,020
It's not in the sense of, you know, I back tested 1,000 sample sets.

38
00:02:39,020 --> 00:02:40,520
It doesn't work like that, okay?

