00:03:45,080 --> 00:03:48,746
So, let's say I'm used to my risk being between minus 100

59
00:03:48,746 --> 00:03:50,412
and, say, minus 200 on average

60
00:03:50,412 --> 00:03:52,412
over a given period of time.

61
00:03:53,080 --> 00:03:54,773
Okay, now, all of a sudden, I decide

62
00:03:54,773 --> 00:03:57,949
I'm going to leverage up and I'm going to go to a four lot, okay?

63
00:03:57,950 --> 00:04:00,165
So, I'm taking on four times the multiple.

64
00:04:00,165 --> 00:04:11,515
Now, instinctively, the minute you have a bad trade, this parameter of 100 to 200 is going to move from 400 to 800, okay?

65
00:04:11,515 --> 00:04:14,347
